  "claim": "The rank of Reichsführer-SS was higher than that of the State Secretary who was in office when Rudolf Plajner was declared Chief Scout of Junák.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Karl Hermann Frank. Sentence: Karl Hermann Frank (24 January 1898 – 22 May 1946) was a prominent Sudeten German Nazi official in Czechoslovakia prior to and during World War II and an SS-\"Obergruppenführer\".\nPage: Obergruppenführer. Sentence: Until April 1942, it was the highest commissioned SS rank, inferior only to \"Reichsführer-SS\" (Heinrich Himmler or RFSS, which was the internal SS-abbreviation for Himmler) Translated as \"senior group leader\", the rank of \"Obergruppenführer\" was senior to \"Gruppenführer\".\nPage: Rudolf Plajner. Sentence: Junák was abolished by force and Scouting prohibited by German State Secretary Karl Hermann Frank during the Nazi occupation of Czechoslovakia on October 28, 1940.",
