      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cad42630-d8a4-5bf4-90a2-b8b05e6b1acf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Karl Hermann Frank, Heinrich Himmler, Rudolf Plajner\n- Organizations: SS, Junák\n- Places: Czechoslovakia\n- Roles: Obergruppenführer, Reichsführer-SS, Gruppenführer\n- Events: Nazi occupation of Czechoslovakia, abolition of Junák\n\nFacts:\n- Karl Hermann Frank was born on 24 January 1898 and died on 22 May 1946.\n- Karl Hermann Frank was a prominent Sudeten German Nazi official in Czechoslovakia before and during World War II.\n- Karl Hermann Frank held the SS rank of Obergruppenführer.\n- Until April 1942, Obergruppenführer was the highest commissioned SS rank below Reichsführer-SS.\n- Heinrich Himmler held the rank Reichsführer-SS, abbreviated internally by the SS as RFSS.\n- Obergruppenführer translates as \"senior group leader\" and ranked above Gruppenführer.\n- During the Nazi occupation of Czechoslovakia, German State Secretary Karl Hermann Frank forcibly abolished Junák and prohibited Scouting on 28 October 1940.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "19ed7104-39c8-583f-8ab6-13020cd1cdf1",
        "text": "Page: Karl Hermann Frank. Sentence: Karl Hermann Frank (24 January 1898 – 22 May 1946) was a prominent Sudeten German Nazi official in Czechoslovakia prior to and during World War II and an SS-\"Obergruppenführer\".\nPage: Obergruppenführer. Sentence: Until April 1942, it was the highest commissioned SS rank, inferior only to \"Reichsführer-SS\" (Heinrich Himmler or RFSS, which was the internal SS-abbreviation for Himmler) Translated as \"senior group leader\", the rank of \"Obergruppenführer\" was senior to \"Gruppenführer\".\nPage: Rudolf Plajner. Sentence: Junák was abolished by force and Scouting prohibited by German State Secretary Karl Hermann Frank during the Nazi occupation of Czechoslovakia on October 28, 1940.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
